# Cloudflare Workers Deployment Guide (OpenNext) — upforge.org

This project is fully configured for deployment to **Cloudflare Workers** using `@opennextjs/cloudflare` and `wrangler`.

---

## 1. Cloudflare Workers Builds Setup (Git Integration)

In the Cloudflare Dashboard (**Workers & Pages -> Create Application -> Git Connection**):

| Setting | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Worker Name** | `upforge-org` |
| **Framework preset** | `None` / `Next.js (OpenNext)` |
| **Build command** | `npx @opennextjs/cloudflare build` |
| **Deploy command** | `npx wrangler deploy` |
| **Root directory** | `/` |

---

## 2. Domain & Custom Domain Configuration (`upforge.org`)

1. Go to **Workers & Pages** → Select `upforge-org` → **Settings** → **Triggers**.
2. Under **Custom Domains**, add:
   - `upforge.org`
   - `www.upforge.org`
3. Cloudflare will automatically provision SSL/TLS certificates and point DNS records directly to your worker.

---

## 3. Environment Variables & Secrets

Environment variables MUST be set in the Cloudflare Dashboard:

> **Cloudflare Dashboard Path**: `Workers & Pages` → `upforge-org` → `Settings` → `Variables and Secrets`

### Required Variables
| Variable Name | Purpose | Used In |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `GROQ_API_KEY` | Groq AI API key for fast inference | `/app/api/chat/route.ts`, `/lib/fallback-ai.ts` |
| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | Google Gemini API key for fallback inference | `/app/api/chat/route.ts`, `/lib/fallback-ai.ts` |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | OpenAI API key for fallback inference | `/lib/fallback-ai.ts` |

---

## 4. Local Development & Deployment Commands

- **Preview Cloudflare Build Locally**:
  ```bash
  pnpm preview
  ```
- **Deploy to Cloudflare via CLI**:
  ```bash
  pnpm deploy
  ```
- **Generate Cloudflare Environment Types**:
  ```bash
  pnpm cf-typegen
  ```

---

## 5. Key File Reference

- `wrangler.jsonc`: Worker entrypoint (`.open-next/worker.js`), `nodejs_compat` flag, ASSETS binding, and custom domain routes (`upforge.org`, `www.upforge.org`).
- `open-next.config.ts`: OpenNext configuration for Cloudflare adapter.
- `next.config.mjs`: Headers, security policies, and domain redirects (`www.upforge.org` → `upforge.org`).
